  <p>
    I'm a data science and mathematics double major at Purdue (class of 2028), and the problems
    that hold my attention are about risk — how to measure it, model it, and see it coming. I
    like math that has to cash out: this past summer that meant upgrading the Value-at-Risk model
    for Cisco's treasury team — Monte Carlo simulation, implied volatility — and building the
    analytics around it.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm also a varsity athlete on Purdue Men's Rowing, which takes about twenty hours a week and
    has taught me more about showing up consistently than anything else I do.
  </p>

  <h2>Outside of work</h2>
  <ul>
